messages:
marta_cs: Jana reported intermittent 403 'scope_mismatch' from mobile SDK during onboarding — spikes when they open ~50+ concurrent sessions. Any quick theories?
kevin_infra: sounds like short-lived ephemeral tokens + concurrency. Could be token rotation or missing scope from issuer. Do we know token TTL and if a proxy is mutating headers?
ryan_sdk: mobile SDK note: iOS process-level token cache can cause fanout if app creates multiple webviews. Also seen when refresh returns older token due to clock skew. What TTL are they using?
marta_cs: Their auth service issues TTL = 30s, via customer proxy -> our gateway. They do parallel warmup calls on launch.
sophia_se: 30s is tight for mobile. Two quick mitigations: increase TTL to ~90-120s, or add a small server-side leeway window to accept slightly older tokens. Also enable SDK preflight to consolidate token ops.
ryan_sdk: agreed. Also recommend SDK change: cache token per app instance + jittered backoff for refresh. Example refresh flow: 
```javascript
async function fetchToken(){
  const r = await fetch('/auth/ephemeral');
  const j = await r.json(); // { token, expires_at, scopes }
  return j;
}
// SDK config hints:
// cacheToken: true, tokenLeewaySeconds: 15, refreshOnNetworkChange: true
```
kevin_infra: I just bumped their burst quota and applied a temporary rate-limiter exception while they test. @rate-limiter-bot FYI
rate-limiter-bot: Rule applied -> customer=acme-inc, burst=200, window=12h. Monitoring enabled.
marta_cs: Customer tested — errors dropped substantially after TTL bump + SDK cache + preflight. They still saw a couple 403s when moving between cellular/wifi. Probably token expiry during aggressive network switch.
sophia_se: For network switch edge case, add a connectivity-change hook to force refresh and small overlap leeway on server (2s-5s). I'll write a short KB entry to include in onboarding checklist.
ryan_sdk: I'll ship a micro-patch to SDK: default tokenLeeway -> 2s, enable jittered backoff, and doc snippet for mobile integrators.
marta_cs: awesome, thanks team :raised_hands: I'll follow up with account owner and mark this thread resolved unless we see regressions.
